I really hate to pick nits, but .... if 'cmevla' is defined by its form ('ends 
in a consonant') the same should apply to at least 'gismu' and probably 'brivla' 


and to 'cmavo'.  Then an added remark about uses might apply. 'bridi' still 
mixes words and things: as words, it is a predicate (selbri) with all its 
arguments(sumti); as things; it describes a relation as holding among the things 


referred to by the sumti (I'd stick with the words part).So a selbri is just the 

predicate expression (refers to a relation) in a bridi, sumti are noun phrases 
(refer to things) in a bridi, a gadri converts a cmevla or nominalized bridi 
into a sumti. (and, while I'm in critical mode, you don't need 'about' after 
'discussing').


